In my Phase 2 project, I focused on refining the emotional tone and visual clarity of my work. Compared to my earlier reflection, this piece shows how I learned to balance concept and composition more intentionally. I adjusted the lighting and color palette to create stronger contrast and mood, making the subject feel more alive and connected to the viewer. The process taught me how small changes — like shifting perspective or emphasizing texture — can completely transform the atmosphere of an image. This reflection captures my growth in understanding how visual storytelling communicates emotion, not just design. It also shows how I’ve become more confident in revising my creative choices to match the message I want the viewer to feel.
